#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-using-vagrant.rst:22
#: 25aebac9f66d4cc4aa41771f55afe3ce
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-using-vagrant.rst:24
#: 77d7730d8ebd41f181bea7331b845519
msgid "The SITL (Software In The Loop) simulator allows you to run Plane, Copter or Rover without any hardware. The simulator runs the normal ArduPilot code as a native executable on a Linux PC. SITL can also be run within a virtual machine on Windows, Mac OSX or Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-using-vagrant.rst:29
#: d2a3db77368f49aa86a6c364dbb08d99
msgid "Vagrant is a tool for automating setting up and configuring development environments running in virtual machines. While it is possible to :ref:`manually set up SITL to run in a VM on Windows <setting-up-sitl-on-windows>` (or Mac OSX), it is **much easier** (and more reproducible) to use Vagrant to do this work for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-using-vagrant.rst:37
#: 9e71ca6786874c49b1f6015b738c410e
msgid "Due to the way submodules are currently handled in the build system, it is not possible to have a repository which can be built on both the host and virtual machines.  A dedicated repository should be used for running the Vagrant virtual machine."
msgstr ""

